    "problem_statement": "Parser returns None for all matches instead of Match/Result objects\n\n#### Description\n\nThe parser is returning None for all string matches instead of returning proper Match or Result objects. This affects all parsing operations and makes the library completely non-functional.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport parse\n\n# Simple parsing that should work\np = parse.compile('hello {:d} {:w}')\nresult = p.parse('hello 12 people')\nprint(result)  # Expected: <Result object>, Actual: None\n\n# Another example\np = parse.compile('{:4}')\nresult = p.parse('looky')\nprint(result)  # Expected: <Result object>, Actual: None\n\n# Even basic patterns fail\np = parse.compile('a {:ti} b')\nresult = p.parse('a 1997-07-16 b')\nprint(result)  # Expected: <Result object>, Actual: None\n```\n\nAll parsing operations return None even when the pattern should match the input string. This breaks all functionality that depends on extracting parsed values from strings."
